Snapshot shared 2D canvas textures before async WebRender handoff on SPARC.

Tab-hover previews draw a PageThumbs ImageBitmap into a chrome 2D canvas and
then display that live canvas in a popup.  The pixels are correct when the
canvas is read back, but forwarding the shared PersistentBufferProvider front
texture directly into the async canvas pipeline can still present a blank
thumbnail with SWGL on Solaris/SPARC.

For shared canvas providers on this platform, use the renderer's existing
snapshot path and copy into a compositor-owned TextureClient.  This keeps the
fix in the canvas/WebRender handoff rather than in browser UI code, and it
preserves the normal zero-copy path for other platforms and non-shared canvas
sources.

Dependency: apply after SPARC-10-canvas-return-target-before-share.patch. The
snapshot handoff assumes shared canvas providers have returned their current
draw target before being forwarded.

